hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1343","Muhammad bin Bashar and Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, they said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Ash’ath bin Sulaym told me. On the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Hilal, on the authority of Tha’labah ibn Zuhdam, he said: We were with Sa’id ibn Al-Aas in Tabaristan, and he said: Which of you prayed with the Messenger of God? May God bless him and grant him peace, the prayer of fear? Hudhayfah said: “I am.” He said: “So Hudhayfah stood up and lined up the people behind him in two rows, one row behind him, parallel to the enemy.” He led those behind him in one rak’ah of prayer, then “These people left in their place, and those people came and he prayed one rak’ah with them, but they did not make up for it.”"
"1344","This is the wording of the hadith of Abu Musa, and Bundar said: On the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi Ash-Sha’atha’, and he did not say: “And they did not make up for it.” He said: He told us, meaning Muhammad, And Abu Musa said: Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Jahm narrated to me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abd. God, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed with Dhu Qard.” Abu Musa said: Like the prayer of Hudhayfah, and he mentioned Bundar narrated the hadith like the hadith of Hudhayfah, and he said at the end of it: And they did not make up for it. Abu Musa said, following the news of Ibn Abbas: Sufyan said: Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, an example of Hudhayfah’s prayer. Bundar told us following the hadith of Hudhayfah, he said: Yahya told us, he said: He told us Sufyan"
"1345","He said: Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan. He said: I asked Zayd bin Thabit about that, and he narrated to me something similar."
"1346","Bishr bin Muadh told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “God made prayer obligatory On the tongue of your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, four rak’ahs in the city, two rak’ahs when traveling, and one rak’ah in fear.”"
